---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PromptPage from "../../../components/PromptPage.astro";

const masterPrompt = `Act as an expert social media copywriter, content strategist and brand voice editor.

TASK:
Write platform-appropriate captions for the supplied content, brand, product, service, creator or campaign.

The caption should:
- support the actual content
- match the target audience
- fit the platform
- reflect the intended tone
- encourage the desired action naturally
- avoid misleading claims
- avoid unnecessary filler
- sound human rather than templated

CONTENT TOPIC:
[What is the post, video, image, carousel or campaign about?]

CONTENT FORMAT:
[Reel / Short / TikTok / image post / carousel / LinkedIn post / Facebook post / YouTube post / other.]

PLATFORM:
[Instagram / Facebook / LinkedIn / TikTok / YouTube / X / other.]

TARGET AUDIENCE:
[Who should this caption speak to?]

AUDIENCE KNOWLEDGE LEVEL:
[Beginner / intermediate / advanced / mixed.]

CONTENT OBJECTIVE:
[Education / engagement / awareness / traffic / leads / sales / community / authority / other.]

CORE MESSAGE:
[What should the audience understand?]

AUDIENCE PROBLEM:
[Optional.]

AUDIENCE DESIRE:
[Optional.]

PRODUCT / SERVICE / OFFER:
[Optional.]

CTA:
[Comment / save / share / follow / click / download / enquire / buy / watch / other.]

BRAND VOICE:
[Professional / conversational / friendly / practical / premium / educational / energetic / warm / direct / other.]

CAPTION LENGTH:
[Short / medium / long / platform-appropriate.]

EMOJI STYLE:
[None / minimal / moderate / expressive.]

HASHTAG STYLE:
[None / minimal / niche / mixed.]

KEYWORDS OR TERMS TO INCLUDE:
[Optional.]

FACTS / CLAIMS:
[Provide verified information that may be used.]

WORDS / PHRASES TO AVOID:
[Optional.]

SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:
[Any additional instructions.]

CAPTION WRITING REQUIREMENTS:

1. UNDERSTAND THE CONTENT BEFORE WRITING

2. IDENTIFY:
Topic
Audience
Objective
Platform
Core message
CTA

3. DO NOT WRITE A GENERIC CAPTION THAT COULD FIT ANY POST

4. THE CAPTION SHOULD ADD CONTEXT, VALUE OR DIRECTION

5. DO NOT SIMPLY REPEAT THE TEXT ALREADY VISIBLE IN THE CONTENT

6. CREATE A STRONG FIRST LINE

7. THE FIRST LINE SHOULD:
Establish relevance
Create interest
Introduce the topic
Or state the main benefit

8. DO NOT USE MISLEADING CLICKBAIT

9. AVOID OVERUSED OPENERS SUCH AS:
"Stop scrolling"
"You won't believe this"
"Nobody talks about this"
"This changes everything"
"Here's the secret"

unless clearly justified.

10. PREFER SPECIFICITY OVER DRAMA

11. MATCH THE PLATFORM

12. INSTAGRAM:
Can be conversational, visual and concise.

13. FACEBOOK:
Can use slightly more context and natural conversation.

14. LINKEDIN:
Should be professional, useful and credible.

15. TIKTOK:
Should feel natural, direct and suited to short-form content.

16. YOUTUBE:
Should support the video topic and next action.

17. DO NOT USE THE SAME CAPTION STRUCTURE FOR EVERY PLATFORM

18. MATCH THE CAPTION TO THE CONTENT FORMAT

19. REEL / SHORT VIDEO:
The caption should complement the video rather than rewrite the spoken script.

20. CAROUSEL:
The caption may introduce the problem and encourage the audience to move through the slides.

21. IMAGE POST:
Add context that the image alone cannot communicate.

22. EDUCATIONAL POST:
Summarize the key takeaway without giving unnecessary filler.

23. PRODUCT POST:
Explain relevance, benefit and next step accurately.

24. CREATE A NATURAL STRUCTURE

25. POSSIBLE STRUCTURE:
Opening
Context
Value
CTA

26. DO NOT FORCE THIS STRUCTURE WHEN A SHORTER CAPTION IS BETTER

27. CREATE SHORT CAPTIONS

28. SHORT CAPTIONS SHOULD:
Be concise
Communicate one idea
Use one clear CTA when needed

29. CREATE MEDIUM CAPTIONS

30. MEDIUM CAPTIONS MAY INCLUDE:
Context
Useful explanation
Key takeaway
CTA

31. CREATE LONG CAPTIONS ONLY WHEN THE CONTENT BENEFITS FROM DEPTH

32. LONG DOES NOT MEAN REPETITIVE

33. REMOVE FILLER

34. REMOVE SENTENCES THAT DO NOT ADD:
Meaning
Context
Emotion
Proof
Instruction
Action

35. USE NATURAL LANGUAGE

36. AVOID ROBOTIC PHRASES SUCH AS:
"In today's fast-paced world"
"Unlock the power of"
"Take your journey to the next level"
"Elevate your experience"

unless the brand genuinely uses that style.

37. AVOID EXCESSIVE MARKETING LANGUAGE

38. USE SIMPLE LANGUAGE WHEN IT IS CLEARER

39. MATCH THE BRAND VOICE

40. PRESERVE TERMINOLOGY THAT MATTERS

41. DO NOT TURN A PROFESSIONAL BRAND INTO A CASUAL MEME ACCOUNT

42. DO NOT MAKE A FRIENDLY BRAND SOUND CORPORATE

43. USE EMOJIS ONLY WHEN THEY FIT

44. DO NOT ADD EMOJIS TO EVERY LINE

45. DO NOT USE EMOJIS AS A SUBSTITUTE FOR CLEAR WRITING

46. IF EMOJIS ARE REQUESTED
Use them intentionally.

47. CREATE CTA OPTIONS

48. CTA SHOULD MATCH THE OBJECTIVE

49. EDUCATIONAL:
Save this
Share with your team
Try this process

50. ENGAGEMENT:
Ask a specific question

51. TRAFFIC:
Read
Watch
Visit
Download

52. LEAD:
Enquire
Book
Request

53. SALES:
Shop
Try
Learn more

54. DO NOT FORCE A SALES CTA ON NON-SALES CONTENT

55. AVOID EMPTY ENGAGEMENT BAIT

56. DO NOT WRITE:
"Comment YES"
"Tag 3 friends"
"Like if you agree"

unless specifically justified.

57. ASK USEFUL QUESTIONS

58. EXAMPLE:
"Which step causes the most stock discrepancies in your operation?"

59. CREATE SAVE CTAS ONLY WHEN THE CONTENT HAS REFERENCE VALUE

60. CREATE SHARE CTAS WHEN THE CONTENT IS USEFUL TO OTHERS

61. USE FOLLOW CTAS SPARINGLY

62. DO NOT ADD:
"Follow for more"
to every caption automatically.

63. CREATE PRODUCT CAPTIONS CAREFULLY

64. ONLY USE FEATURES PROVIDED

65. DO NOT INVENT:
Benefits
Materials
Specifications
Availability
Pricing
Discounts
Guarantees

66. CREATE SERVICE CAPTIONS CAREFULLY

67. DO NOT INVENT:
Experience
Results
Customer numbers
Case studies
Turnaround times

68. CREATE PROMOTIONAL CAPTIONS

69. PROMOTIONAL CAPTIONS SHOULD CLEARLY EXPLAIN:
What is offered
Who it is for
Why it matters
What action to take

70. DO NOT USE FALSE URGENCY

71. DO NOT INVENT:
"Last chance"
"Only today"
"Limited spots"
"Almost sold out"

unless verified.

72. DO NOT CREATE FALSE SCARCITY

73. DO NOT INVENT SOCIAL PROOF

74. DO NOT INVENT:
Ratings
Reviews
Customer quotes
Testimonials
Sales numbers
User counts

75. DO NOT INVENT STATISTICS

76. DO NOT INVENT RESEARCH FINDINGS

77. DO NOT INVENT INDUSTRY TRENDS

78. PRESERVE VERIFIED NUMBERS EXACTLY

79. FLAG UNSUPPORTED CLAIMS

80. CREATE EDUCATIONAL CAPTIONS

81. EDUCATIONAL CAPTIONS SHOULD:
Explain
Clarify
Demonstrate
Correct misunderstanding

82. DO NOT SOUND LIKE A LECTURE UNLESS APPROPRIATE

83. CREATE EXPERT / AUTHORITY CAPTIONS

84. AUTHORITY SHOULD COME FROM:
Useful explanation
Judgment
Experience provided
Clear methodology

85. DO NOT USE SELF-PROMOTIONAL CLAIMS WITHOUT BASIS

86. CREATE STORY CAPTIONS ONLY WHEN A REAL STORY IS PROVIDED

87. DO NOT FABRICATE:
Personal experiences
Customer stories
Behind-the-scenes events

88. IF A HYPOTHETICAL EXAMPLE IS USED
Label it clearly.

89. CREATE BEFORE / AFTER CAPTIONS ONLY WHEN THE CHANGE IS REAL

90. DO NOT EXAGGERATE OUTCOMES

91. CREATE COMPARISON CAPTIONS CAREFULLY

92. COMPARE USING ACTUAL CRITERIA

93. DO NOT CREATE FALSE WINNERS

94. CREATE QUESTION-LED CAPTIONS

95. QUESTIONS SHOULD BE SPECIFIC

96. BAD:
"Do you want better results?"

97. BETTER:
"What do you check first when physical inventory doesn't match the system?"

98. CREATE PROBLEM-LED CAPTIONS

99. NAME A REALISTIC PROBLEM

100. DO NOT USE FEAR UNNECESSARILY

101. CREATE OUTCOME-LED CAPTIONS

102. OUTCOMES MUST BE PLAUSIBLE

103. DO NOT GUARANTEE SUCCESS

104. CREATE MISTAKE-LED CAPTIONS

105. EXPLAIN A REAL MISTAKE

106. DO NOT SHAME THE AUDIENCE

107. CREATE CHECKLIST CAPTIONS

108. IF USING A NUMBER
Ensure the content contains that exact number of points.

109. DO NOT WRITE:
"5 tips"
if only 4 tips exist.

110. CREATE LIST CAPTIONS WHEN THEY HELP SCANNABILITY

111. DO NOT BREAK EVERY SENTENCE INTO A SEPARATE LINE

112. USE PARAGRAPH SPACING NATURALLY

113. CREATE HOOK VARIANTS

114. GENERATE DIFFERENT ANGLES, NOT SYNONYMS

115. POSSIBLE ANGLES:
Problem
Question
Outcome
Mistake
Observation
Checklist
Comparison
Insight

116. CREATE PLATFORM VARIANTS

117. IF MULTIPLE PLATFORMS ARE REQUESTED
Adapt:
Opening
Length
Tone
CTA
Formatting

118. DO NOT JUST COPY THE SAME CAPTION ACROSS PLATFORMS

119. CREATE HASHTAGS CAREFULLY

120. ONLY INCLUDE HASHTAGS WHEN REQUESTED OR PLATFORM-APPROPRIATE

121. PREFER RELEVANT HASHTAGS OVER LARGE GENERIC LISTS

122. DO NOT CLAIM HASHTAGS ARE TRENDING WITHOUT CURRENT DATA

123. DO NOT GENERATE 30 HASHTAGS AUTOMATICALLY

124. DEFAULT TO A SMALL RELEVANT SET

125. CREATE KEYWORD-AWARE CAPTIONS WHEN USEFUL

126. INCORPORATE TERMS NATURALLY

127. DO NOT KEYWORD-STUFF

128. CREATE ACCESSIBLE LANGUAGE

129. IF IMPORTANT CONTEXT IS ONLY VISUAL
Consider mentioning it briefly in the caption.

130. DO NOT ATTEMPT TO REPLACE PROPER ALT TEXT WHEN ALT TEXT IS SUPPORTED

131. CREATE MULTILINGUAL CAPTIONS WHEN REQUESTED

132. PRESERVE:
Meaning
Tone
Product names
Technical terms

133. DO NOT TRANSLATE WORD-FOR-WORD WHEN NATURAL LOCAL LANGUAGE IS BETTER

134. CREATE CAPTION LENGTH VARIANTS

135. PROVIDE:
Short
Medium
Long

when useful.

136. CREATE A "CLEAN VERSION"

137. CLEAN VERSION SHOULD REMOVE:
Unnecessary emojis
Hashtags
Marketing clichés
Excessive punctuation

138. CREATE A "WARM VERSION" WHEN APPROPRIATE

139. CREATE A "PROFESSIONAL VERSION" WHEN APPROPRIATE

140. CREATE A "CONVERSION VERSION" ONLY WHEN A CONVERSION GOAL EXISTS

141. CREATE A CAPTION QUALITY CHECK

142. REVIEW:
Relevance
Clarity
Brand fit
Credibility
Platform fit
CTA fit

143. USE:
Strong
Good
Needs revision

144. DO NOT CREATE FALSE NUMERICAL SCORES

145. IDENTIFY CLAIM RISKS

146. FLAG:
Unverified statistics
Unsupported outcomes
Health claims
Financial claims
Legal claims
Safety claims
Current product information

147. PROVIDE SAFER WORDING WHEN NEEDED

148. CREATE A/B TEST OPTIONS

149. CHANGE ONE MAIN VARIABLE

150. POSSIBLE TEST:
Question opening vs statement opening

151. DO NOT GUARANTEE WHICH WILL PERFORM BETTER

152. CREATE COMMENT RESPONSE OPPORTUNITIES

153. WHEN RELEVANT
Suggest 3 likely audience follow-up questions the creator may need to answer.

154. DO NOT INVENT ACTUAL COMMENTS

155. CREATE REPURPOSING VARIANTS

156. ONE CONTENT PIECE MAY NEED:
LinkedIn caption
Facebook caption
Instagram caption
Short-video caption

157. ADAPT EACH VERSION NATIVELY

158. CREATE SENSITIVE-TOPIC CAUTION

159. FOR:
Health
Finance
Legal
Safety

avoid presenting unverified advice as authoritative fact.

160. CREATE FACT-CHECK FLAGS

161. USE:
[VERIFY CLAIM]

where supporting evidence is required.

162. CREATE FINAL PUBLISHING VERSION

163. THE FINAL VERSION SHOULD:
Be ready to copy
Use clean formatting
Contain no instructional placeholders
Contain no explanations inside the caption

164. FINAL QUALITY CHECK
Before finalizing verify:

- caption matches the actual content
- opening is relevant
- platform fit is strong
- audience language is appropriate
- brand voice is preserved
- caption adds value rather than repeating the visual
- no facts are invented
- no statistics are invented
- no testimonials are invented
- no fake urgency is used
- no false scarcity is used
- CTA matches the objective
- hashtags are relevant if included
- emojis are intentional if included
- wording is natural
- important claims are flagged
- final version is ready to publish

OUTPUT FORMAT:

1. CAPTION STRATEGY
Provide:
Platform
Audience
Objective
Core message
Recommended tone
Recommended caption length
Best CTA direction

2. OPENING OPTIONS
Provide 5–10 first-line options using different angles.

3. PRIMARY CAPTION
Write the recommended platform-ready caption.

4. SHORT VERSION
Create a concise alternative.

5. MEDIUM VERSION
Create a balanced alternative.

6. LONG VERSION
Create only if useful.

7. PROFESSIONAL VERSION
Create when relevant.

8. CONVERSATIONAL VERSION
Create when relevant.

9. ENGAGEMENT VERSION
Create when relevant.

10. CONVERSION VERSION
Create only if the objective supports it.

11. PLATFORM VARIANTS
If multiple platforms are requested, create a native caption for each.

12. CTA OPTIONS
Provide 3–5 relevant CTA choices.

13. HASHTAGS
Provide a small, relevant set only if requested or useful.

14. CLAIM REVIEW
List:
Claim
Evidence status
Safer wording if required

15. A/B TEST
Provide:
Version A
Version B
Variable tested

16. POSSIBLE FOLLOW-UP QUESTIONS
Provide 3 likely audience questions when useful.

17. FINAL PUBLISHING VERSION
Provide the strongest clean caption ready to copy and post.

IMPORTANT:
- Do not fabricate facts, testimonials, trends, results or statistics.
- Do not use false urgency or scarcity.
- Match the actual content and platform.
- Use human, natural language.
- Prioritize relevance and clarity over hype.`;

const steps = [
  {
    title: "Start with the actual content",
    description:
      "The caption should support the post, video or image rather than becoming a generic paragraph that could be attached to almost anything.",
  },
  {
    title: "Match the platform and audience",
    description:
      "Adjust the opening, length, tone, formatting and CTA for the audience and platform instead of copying the same caption everywhere.",
  },
  {
    title: "Add value beyond the visual",
    description:
      "Use the caption for context, explanation, a useful takeaway or a clear next step rather than simply repeating what viewers already see.",
  },
  {
    title: "Review credibility before posting",
    description:
      "Remove invented claims, unsupported outcomes, false urgency and unnecessary hype, then make sure the final CTA fits the content objective.",
  },
];

const example = {
  input: [
    "Platform: LinkedIn.",
    "Topic: Physical stock does not match the inventory system.",
    "Audience: Warehouse supervisors and inventory controllers.",
    "Objective: Educational authority.",
    "Tone: Practical and professional.",
    "CTA: Encourage discussion.",
  ],

  output: [
    "OPENING: 'An inventory adjustment can correct the number without correcting the problem.'",
    "CAPTION: 'When physical stock does not match the system, the first response should not always be to adjust the quantity. Start by confirming the count, then review recent receipts, transfers, picks, returns and previous adjustments. The objective is not only to correct the stock balance, but to understand what caused the discrepancy so the same issue does not keep returning.'",
    "CTA: 'Which area do you normally investigate first when a stock discrepancy appears?'",
    "STYLE: Professional, useful and specific without exaggerated claims or unnecessary hashtags.",
  ],
};

const tips = [
  {
    title: "Do not make the caption duplicate the content",
    description:
      "A strong caption adds context, meaning or a next step. If the video already explains everything, the caption can stay shorter.",
  },
  {
    title: "One clear CTA is usually enough",
    description:
      "Asking people to like, save, share, follow, comment and click at the same time weakens the main action you actually want them to take.",
  },
  {
    title: "Platform adaptation matters",
    description:
      "The same message can be professional on LinkedIn, conversational on Facebook and much shorter on a Reel without changing the underlying facts.",
  },
];

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Caption Writer Prompt | KRIYANO"
  description="Write natural, platform-specific social media captions for Reels, posts, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok and YouTube."
>
  <PromptPage
    category="CREATORS"
    title="Caption Writer"
    accentTitle="Prompt."
    description="Create natural, platform-aware captions that support the actual content, match your brand voice and encourage the right action without relying on generic filler or misleading hype."
    meta={[
      "Free prompt",
      "Social captions",
      "Multi-platform",
    ]}
    bestFor={[
      "Instagram",
      "Facebook",
      "LinkedIn",
      "Reels & Shorts",
      "TikTok",
      "YouTube",
    ]}
    masterPrompt={masterPrompt}
    introTitle="Turn the content into a caption worth reading."
    introDescription="Define the platform, audience, message and objective, then create a caption that adds useful context, preserves the brand voice and ends with a natural next step."
    steps={steps}
    exampleTitle="Write a professional caption around an inventory-control lesson."
    example={example}
    tipsTitle="Good captions support the content instead of competing with it."
    tips={tips}
    sidebarTitle="Need a stronger opening?"
    sidebarDescription="Use KRIYANO's Hook Generator for first-line options, or Content Repurposing Prompt when the same piece of content needs native captions for several platforms."
    warningTitle="Keep promotional claims accurate"
    warningText="Do not invent statistics, customer results, reviews, discounts, availability, urgency or scarcity. Verify fact-sensitive claims before publishing and keep the caption consistent with what the actual content or offer can deliver."
  />
</BaseLayout>